# Forms & Validation

## Form library — not yet decided/installed

Neither `react-hook-form` nor `yup` (nor `@hookform/resolvers`) is currently
in `package.json` — this file documents the React Hook Form + Yup pattern as
the working convention *if/when* a form library is adopted, matching how
`.claude/workflows/create-form.md` treats the form-library choice as not yet
finalized. Don't `import` from either package without first confirming it's
actually installed; if you're building the first real form in this repo,
that's the moment to add the dependency deliberately (and note it here),
not to assume it's already there.

## React Hook Form + Yup Integration (target pattern)

### Login Form
```javascript
// src/components/auth/LoginForm.jsx
import React from 'react'
import { useForm, Controller } from 'react-hook-form'
import { yupResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/yup'
import * as yup from 'yup'
import {
  Button,
  TextField,
  Box,
  Typography
} from '@mui/material'

// Validation schema — matches POST /auth/login body exactly
const loginSchema = yup.object({
  email: yup
    .string()
    .required('Email is required')
    .email('Enter a valid email address'),
  password: yup
    .string()
    .required('Password is required')
})

const LoginForm = ({ onSubmit, loading = false, serverError }) => {
  const {
    control,
    handleSubmit,
    formState: { errors, isSubmitting }
  } = useForm({
    resolver: yupResolver(loginSchema),
    defaultValues: { email: '', password: '' }
  })

  const handleFormSubmit = async (data) => {
    // Container attaches deviceId (client-generated, persisted in
    // localStorage) and deviceType: 'WEB' before calling the API —
    // this form only collects email/password.
    await onSubmit(data)
  }

  return (
    <Box component="form" onSubmit={handleSubmit(handleFormSubmit)}>
      <Typography variant="h6" gutterBottom>
        Log In
      </Typography>

      <Controller
        name="email"
        control={control}
        render={({ field }) => (
          <TextField
            {...field}
            label="Email"
            type="email"
            error={!!errors.email}
            helperText={errors.email?.message}
            fullWidth
            margin="normal"
          />
        )}
      />

      <Controller
        name="password"
        control={control}
        render={({ field }) => (
          <TextField
            {...field}
            label="Password"
            type="password"
            error={!!errors.password}
            helperText={errors.password?.message}
            fullWidth
            margin="normal"
          />
        )}
      />

      {serverError && (
        <Typography color="error" variant="body2" sx={{ mt: 1 }}>
          {serverError}
        </Typography>
      )}

      <Button
        type="submit"
        variant="contained"
        fullWidth
        disabled={isSubmitting || loading}
        sx={{ mt: 3, mb: 2 }}
      >
        {isSubmitting || loading ? 'Logging in...' : 'Log In'}
      </Button>
    </Box>
  )
}

export default LoginForm
```

## Auth-Specific Form Schemas

These match `docs/AUTH_MODULE.md`'s request bodies exactly — see
[[06-auth-security]] for the full endpoint contract. Don't invent extra
fields or a different shape.

### Register Schema
```javascript
// src/schemas/registerSchema.js
import * as yup from 'yup'

// POST /auth/register — { username, email, password }
export const registerSchema = yup.object({
  username: yup
    .string()
    .required('Username is required')
    .min(3, 'Username must be at least 3 characters')
    .max(30, 'Username must be less than 30 characters'),
  email: yup
    .string()
    .required('Email is required')
    .email('Enter a valid email address'),
  password: yup
    .string()
    .required('Password is required')
    .min(8, 'Password must be at least 8 characters')
})
```

### Login Schema
```javascript
// src/schemas/loginSchema.js
import * as yup from 'yup'

// POST /auth/login — { email, password, deviceId, deviceType }
// deviceId/deviceType are attached by the container, not collected in the form
export const loginSchema = yup.object({
  email: yup.string().required('Email is required').email('Enter a valid email address'),
  password: yup.string().required('Password is required')
})
```

### OTP Verification Schema
```javascript
// src/schemas/otpSchema.js
import * as yup from 'yup'

// POST /auth/verify-otp — { email, otp, deviceId, deviceType }
export const otpSchema = yup.object({
  email: yup.string().required().email(),
  otp: yup
    .string()
    .required('Enter the 6-digit code')
    .matches(/^[0-9]{6}$/, 'Code must be exactly 6 digits')
})
```

## OTP Verification Form

```javascript
// src/components/auth/OTPVerificationForm.jsx
import React from 'react'
import { useForm, Controller } from 'react-hook-form'
import { yupResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/yup'
import { Button, TextField, Box, Typography } from '@mui/material'
import { otpSchema } from 'schemas/otpSchema'

const OTPVerificationForm = ({ email, onSubmit, onResend, loading = false }) => {
  const {
    control,
    handleSubmit,
    formState: { errors, isSubmitting }
  } = useForm({
    resolver: yupResolver(otpSchema),
    defaultValues: { email, otp: '' }
  })

  return (
    <Box component="form" onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
      <Typography variant="h6" gutterBottom>
        Verify your email
      </Typography>
      <Typography variant="body2" color="text.secondary" sx={{ mb: 2 }}>
        Enter the 6-digit code sent to {email}
      </Typography>

      <Controller
        name="otp"
        control={control}
        render={({ field }) => (
          <TextField
            {...field}
            label="Verification code"
            inputProps={{ maxLength: 6, inputMode: 'numeric' }}
            error={!!errors.otp}
            helperText={errors.otp?.message}
            fullWidth
            margin="normal"
          />
        )}
      />

      <Button
        type="submit"
        variant="contained"
        fullWidth
        disabled={isSubmitting || loading}
        sx={{ mt: 2, mb: 1 }}
      >
        {isSubmitting || loading ? 'Verifying...' : 'Verify'}
      </Button>

      <Button onClick={onResend} fullWidth>
        Resend code
      </Button>
    </Box>
  )
}

export default OTPVerificationForm
```

## Form State Management

### Loading States
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - Proper loading state management
const RegisterForm = ({ onSubmit }) => {
  const [isSubmitting, setIsSubmitting] = useState(false)
  const [submitError, setSubmitError] = useState(null)

  const {
    control,
    handleSubmit,
    formState: { errors, isValid },
    reset
  } = useForm({
    resolver: yupResolver(registerSchema),
    mode: 'onChange' // Validate on change for better UX
  })

  const handleFormSubmit = async (data) => {
    setIsSubmitting(true)
    setSubmitError(null)

    try {
      await onSubmit(data)
      reset() // Clear form on success
    } catch (error) {
      // Map server error codes (EMAIL_TAKEN, OTP_COOLDOWN) to a friendly message
      setSubmitError(error.message || 'Registration failed')
    } finally {
      setIsSubmitting(false)
    }
  }

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(handleFormSubmit)}>
      {/* Form fields */}

      {submitError && (
        <Alert severity="error" sx={{ mt: 2 }}>
          {submitError}
        </Alert>
      )}

      <Button type="submit" disabled={!isValid || isSubmitting} fullWidth>
        {isSubmitting ? 'Processing...' : 'Submit'}
      </Button>
    </form>
  )
}
```

### Error Handling — mapping server error codes
`docs/AUTH_MODULE.md` returns specific error codes rather than free-form
messages (`EMAIL_TAKEN`, `OTP_INVALID`, `INVALID_CREDENTIALS`,
`EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED`, `OTP_COOLDOWN`, `USER_NOT_FOUND`). Map these to
field-level or form-level errors rather than showing the raw code:

```javascript
// ✅ Correct - Map known error codes to field errors
const handleServerError = (setError, code) => {
  switch (code) {
    case 'EMAIL_TAKEN':
      setError('email', { type: 'server', message: 'This email is already registered' })
      break
    case 'INVALID_CREDENTIALS':
      setError('password', { type: 'server', message: 'Incorrect email or password' })
      break
    case 'EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED':
      setError('email', { type: 'server', message: 'Please verify your email first' })
      break
    case 'OTP_INVALID':
      setError('otp', { type: 'server', message: 'Invalid or expired code' })
      break
    case 'OTP_COOLDOWN':
      setError('otp', { type: 'server', message: 'Please wait before requesting another code' })
      break
    default:
      // Fall back to a toast (sonner) for unmapped/unexpected errors
      break
  }
}
```

## Form Accessibility

### ARIA Labels and Roles
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - Accessible form elements
const AccessibleLoginForm = () => {
  return (
    <form role="form" aria-label="Login form">
      <TextField
        label="Email"
        aria-describedby="email-help"
        aria-required="true"
        error={!!errors.email}
        helperText={errors.email?.message}
      />

      <div id="email-help">
        Use the email address you registered with
      </div>

      <Button type="submit" aria-label="Submit login form" disabled={isSubmitting}>
        {isSubmitting ? 'Logging in...' : 'Log In'}
      </Button>
    </form>
  )
}
```

## Form Requirements Checklist

### ✅ Basic Requirements
- [ ] Confirm `react-hook-form`/`yup` are actually installed before using them
- [ ] Use React Hook Form for form management
- [ ] Include a Yup validation schema matching the exact server request body
- [ ] Use `Controller` for MUI components
- [ ] Add proper error handling and display, including mapped server error codes
- [ ] Include loading states during submission
- [ ] Disable submit button when form is invalid
- [ ] Use PropTypes for all prop validation (NO TypeScript)
- [ ] Follow JSX file structure order (see [[02-code-standards]])

### ✅ User Experience
- [ ] Provide clear field labels and placeholders
- [ ] Include helpful text and examples
- [ ] Add progress indicators for multi-step forms (register → OTP)
- [ ] Add form reset functionality
- [ ] Use MUI SX prop for all styling needs

### ✅ Accessibility
- [ ] Include proper ARIA labels
- [ ] Ensure keyboard navigation works
- [ ] Add screen reader support
- [ ] Include proper focus management
- [ ] Test with accessibility tools
